  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responsive Stabilisation Through Transition (RESET)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project, led by Mercy Corps through a consortium of NGOs and one UN partner, delivers governance-focused, area-based stabilisation to strengthen local peace and security in eastern Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC). This includes training for law enforcement and community actors in conflict management and dialogue, facilitating democratic dialogue on the causes of conflict and provides socio-economic opportunities for marginalised groups and ex-combatants. Its activities are aligned with the provincial operational plans of the DRC&#x2019;s Disarmament, Demobilisation, Community Recovery and Stabilisation Programme (PDDRCS), and are coordinated with key stabilisation actors including the World Bank, the EU, the UN Stabilisation and Coherence Fund, UNDP&#x2019;s Stabilisation Pillar, USAID, and other bilateral donors.</narrative>
  </description>
